UID:oYC9ZKflk080MirHSsZBr
SUMMARY:Historic Glenwood Cemetery Part II walking tour: Houston After Oil
DTSTAMP:20260722T105546Z
DTSTART:20260926T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Please note that advance ticket purchase is required for this t
	our.Glenwood Cemetery\, established in 1871 on rolling\, wooded land near 
	Buffalo Bayou\, is one of the most beautiful outdoor spaces in Houston. It
	 is also the resting place of scores of people who built Houston into the 
	city we know today. This two-hour docent-guided tour looks at the lives an
	d legacies of some of the men and women buried at Glenwood who shaped Hous
	ton after the turn of the 20th century.\n\nhttps://www.preservationhouston
